arm64: dts: r4-pro: boot-time SFP media for both 8X combo ports

Both 10G combo ports route one SerDes through a CM17 mux to either the
AS21010P copper PHY or an SFP+ cage: GPIO3 for the WAN combo (MT7988
USXGMII_1, eth1) and GPIO54 for the LAN combo (MxL SerDes port 13,
mxl_lan4). The cages use the same nets as the 4E: SFP2 on PCA9545 channel 2
with GPIO1/2/0 for MOD_ABS/LOS/TX_DISABLE, SFP1 on channel 1 with
GPIO69/70/21.

The base DTB stays the copper board unchanged, because environments that
predate the media selector apply no media overlay. An overlay cannot delete
the copper phy-handle, so each SFP attachment is a second, disabled node for
the same MAC id or switch port, next to a disabled mux hog. The wan-sfp and
lan-sfp overlays swap which node and hog are enabled and set
/chosen/bpirouter,{wan,lan}-media; netdev names follow the MAC id and the
port label, so eth1 and mxl_lan4 keep their names on either medium. The
AS21010P nodes stay enabled; the PHY preparation service (469) reads the
/chosen media and leaves the PHY of a combo booted on SFP untouched.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x.dts
